  "foot": { "text": "RAS falls when DRAM_REGION_ACCESS clocks nDRAM_ACCESS_RAS. DRAM_MUX is clocked by the RAS pins falling, so the row address is held about 2 slots. CAS starts from RAS_RESET1 on the first falling edge after RAS, and RAS_RESET2 ends RAS one clock later while CAS stays low until AS negates. DSACK comes from the falling-edge WAITSTATE flop, giving 4-clock DRAM cycles. Diagram is schematic (1 slot = 12.5 ns, about one CPLD step); see docs/DRAM.md for the nanosecond budget." },
